The  field  is  the  number  of seconds from the epoch, until the
password for the account must be changed.  This field may be left
empty to turn off the password aging feature.  If this is set  to
then  the  user  will be prompted to change their password at the
next login.  The field is the number of seconds from  the  epoch,
until  the account expires.  This field may be left empty to turn
off the account aging feature.  If either of the  or  fields  are
set,  the  system will remind the user of the impending change or
expiry if they login within a configurable period (defaulting  to
14  days)  before  the  event.  The field normally contains comma
separated subfields as follows: user’s full  name  user’s  office
number user’s work phone number user’s home phone number The full
name may contain an ampersand which will be replaced by the capi‐
talized  login  name when the gecos field is displayed or used by
various programs such as etc.  The office and phone  number  sub‐
fields  are used by the program, and possibly other applications.
The user’s home directory is the full path name  where  the  user
will  be  placed on login.  The shell field is the command inter‐
preter the user prefers.  If there is nothing in the  field,  the
